cff-version: 1.2.0
title: depvet — vet every dependency before your agent installs it
message: >-
  If you use depvet, please cite it using this metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - name: TusharB-07
repository-code: "https://github.com/TusharB-07/depvet"
url: "https://github.com/TusharB-07/depvet"
abstract: >-
  An Agent Skills compatible skill that gates dependency installation for AI
  coding agents. Vets npm and PyPI packages — individually or from whole
  package-lock.json / requirements.txt manifests — for typosquats,
  slopsquats, confusable identities, dangerous lifecycle scripts, deprecation,
  abandonment, and license gaps before an install command runs. Also ships
  as a reusable GitHub Action (TusharB-07/depvet@v1) for PR-level gating.
keywords:
  - agent-skills
  - supply-chain-security
  - typosquatting
  - slopsquatting
  - npm
  - pypi
license: MIT
version: 1.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-11"
